            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed the full candidate for security, data exposure, unsafe input handling, secrets and dependency risk.",
              "The generator reads only fixed role source paths under the repository root, which comes from OVERLAY_DIR, and writes only fixed table paths. No user-controlled path segments are involved, so there is no traversal or injection surface.",
              "The TOML writer escapes backslashes and triple-quote runs and refuses control characters, so a role source cannot break out of the string or write a malformed Codex file.",
              "The CI step passes only github.workspace as an environment variable and adds no secrets or untrusted inputs.",
              "The change adds no dependencies and no network access.",
              "The reviewer agent loses its Engram line only because it has no Engram tool, which narrows its access and does not widen it."
            ]
          }
        }
